meta {
  name: Update Family Attribute Level
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

patch {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families/REPLACE_WITH_FAMILY_ID/attributes/REPLACE_WITH_ATTRIBUTE_ID
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "level": "parent_level"
  }
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 against the disposable scratch product family
  from "Create Family Attribute Link.bru" (id `6aa97212a30ca5945169a21e`)
  and the Phase 1 kept text-attribute fixture (id
  `6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1`) on "David's Dev Account". Brand-new
  endpoint in the 2026-09-15 `openapi_pimv3.json` refresh.

  ## Real finding -- a genuine account-level feature gate
  Attempting to change an attribute's `level` (e.g. from `no_level` to
  `parent_level`, which implies moving the attribute's values up to the
  parent and having variants inherit them) returned `403
  {"errors":[{"name":"PermissionError","description":"Automatic
  inheritance is not available for this account"}]}` -- **not** a 422
  validation error, a distinct 403 permission-error shape not seen
  anywhere else in this project. This reads as a real account-tier
  feature flag (attribute-level automatic inheritance), not a request
  bug. Add this account to the status-gating rules in
  `config/api-testing.config.md` -- untestable further without a
  different account/plan tier.

  This means the success shape of this PATCH (what the response looks
  like when the level change is actually applied) remains **unconfirmed**
  in this account -- flag as an open item, same category as the
  PDF Catalogs/Ecatalogs feature gates (status-gating #2/#3).
}

example {
  name: Update Family Attribute Level - Feature Not Enabled (403)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15 -- the only response shape this account can produce for this operation.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families/6aa97212a30ca5945169a21e/attributes/6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1
    method: patch
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "level": "parent_level"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 403
      text: Forbidden
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "PermissionError",
              "description": "Automatic inheritance is not available for this account"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
